<title>USA: USDA--karnal bunt spores in 7 Georgia counties.</title>
<headline>USDA--karnal bunt spores in 7 Georgia counties.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The ongoing national karnal bunt survey discovered teliospores, the causal agent for the wheat fungus, in wheat samples from seven counties in Georgia, the U.S. Agriculture Department said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The seven counties were Morgan, Houston, Greene, Jackson, Jasper, Johnson and Macon.</p>
<p>USDA said it would take &quot;those administrative and regulatory actions necessary to conduct the full range of appropriate containment and eradication measures.&quot;</p>
</text>
